+/*
+ * arm64: the access is one A64 load or store, and the instruction set makes
+ * that simpler than x86 -- a read-modify-write or a compare against memory is
+ * a separate load and store, each faulting on its own, so only the load/store
+ * classes are decoded. Covered: LDR/STR of every width and signedness in the
+ * unsigned-offset, unscaled, pre/post-index and register-offset forms, the
+ * same for scalar FP/SIMD registers, LDP/STP/LDPSW, and the ordered forms
+ * the generated code's accessors compile to (LDAR/LDAPR/STLR and the
+ * unscaled LDAPUR/LDAPURS/STLUR). Exclusive and atomic read-modify-write
+ * forms are refused (return 0), as is anything else.
